# Which dist set each installed path belongs to (OxideBSD-doc RAM_FLOOR.md §4.3.2), as NetBSD's
# distrib/sets/lists do. One pattern per line: `*` matches within a path component, `**` any
# number of components. A path belongs to the set whose matching pattern is the most specific:
# an exact path over any pattern, then the longer pattern. A path no list claims, or two claim
# equally, fails the build.
#
# base: everything a console install runs (§1).
.
./bin
./bin/**
./boot
./boot/**
./cdrom
./dev
./proc
./etc
./etc/**
./home
./home/**
./lib
./lib/**
